WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:29.970
Was it my dream to become a spy?

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:32.220
No, it wasn't my dream to become a spy.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:33.380
I was very young.

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:37.930
I never thought about spying,
or spies, or the spying world.

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:40.420
Yes, it was the job that chose me.

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:43.250
How did I find out that I was recruited?

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:46.090
The first day of school,
eight o'clock in the morning,

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:48.104
and the big man at the head of the table

00:00:48.104 --> 00:00:50.650
said, "Welcome to the Institute."

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:51.680
And I was shocked.

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:56.513
I couldn't believe it, I really
almost fell off the chair.

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:05.740
The first day that I came
and they told me where I was,

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:10.290
I said, "Why was I
accepted to this school?"

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:11.463
It didn't seem logical.

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:14.300
What made me suitable for the job

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:17.340
was things that they saw in me

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:20.069
that I didn't even know about myself.

00:01:20.069 --> 00:01:24.330
The strength, the ability to be by myself,

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:26.390
the ability to be open-minded,

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:28.840
to see things through, to understand them,

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:31.590
to see people and understand who they are

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:33.350
and what to expect of them.

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:34.890
Things like that.

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:36.927
When I recruited people,
when I asked them,

00:01:36.927 --> 00:01:39.770
"What do you think you
need to become a spy?"

00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:42.660
Many people say you have to be fearless.

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:44.750
So I say, "No, no, no.

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:48.300
You have to be afraid because
it's one of your tools."

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:51.280
When you feel fear, you
have to translate it.

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:52.740
Is it connected to you?

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:55.000
Is it connected to the surroundings?

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.020
Or if it comes from your instincts

00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:59.580
about the mission, about the job,

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:02.420
then you have to take it
seriously and understand it.

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:04.510
You must feel the fear,

00:02:04.510 --> 00:02:08.090
but you must continue doing
what you do with that fear.

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:09.980
If you're stopped by the fear,

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:13.397
that means you're not suited for the job.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:29.410
I wasn't really finished
with studying and school.

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:31.274
But I was needed, because at that time

00:02:31.274 --> 00:02:33.580
there were hardly any women on the job.

00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:35.450
They needed a woman and I went.

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:39.360
We got to the airport and first
thing is passport control.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:42.890
And I'm standing in the
queue and I'm scared.

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:45.559
And I realized that I
couldn't remember my name,

00:02:45.559 --> 00:02:48.320
the name in the passport.

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:49.540
It took me awhile.

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:52.360
Took me a few seconds, a minute.

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:54.530
I don't even know how long it was.

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:56.160
But then I thought about it,

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:58.290
calmed down, remembered my name,

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:00.660
and went through passport control.

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:03.810
Second time was not really
scared, but nervous.

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:06.903
And the third time, I really
did it with no problem.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:09.840
Normally you just go through it.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:11.940
You do what you need to do.

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:13.990
Can you teach somebody not to be scared?

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:15.260
You can try.

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:17.900
You need to know how to manage your fear.

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:19.770
In order to manage your fear,

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:22.840
you need to be very
focused and to understand

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:25.790
what you're doing there
and why you're there.

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:28.030
You need to control the fear.

00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:31.620
Some things you can't teach,
you can teach technical things.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:35.700
You can teach people how
to speak a proper language,

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:38.160
proper accent, how to follow people,

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:40.940
how to find out if you are being followed,

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:43.030
how to take good photos.

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:45.880
You can learn lots of things,
which I will not go into,

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:49.603
but these are the skills of being a spy.

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:52.420
And the rest is you.

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:54.400
In this job, everybody's different,

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.010
I mean, we're all different.

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:58.490
I don't think you'll
find one person similar

00:03:58.490 --> 00:04:00.710
or exactly the same like the other.

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:03.560
The Institute uses
differences between people

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:06.840
because you have so many missions,

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:10.660
so many different people
to do different jobs.

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:14.410
Everybody has their own
way to play the game.

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:30.740
When you go on a mission,

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:32.480
you need to know that you might be caught.

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:36.100
You might find yourself
interrogated, being tortured even.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:39.200
Can you prepare yourself
to be interrogated?

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:40.700
Yes, you can.

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:42.340
But when it's for real,

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:46.750
you never know how you will
react at the real moment.

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:50.593
The Institute always knows
that you might speak.

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:53.830
And you can look back at
stories that happened,

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:57.380
people were caught, and
people told their stories

00:04:57.380 --> 00:04:58.373
and some didn't.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:00.600
It's not a fantasy.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:03.827
There is fear and the rest is you.

